\title{By the arena rule the machine as default engine is worth seven places, the shortcuts two more}
\taxon{Insight}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{arena}
\tag{benchmark}
\tag{machine}
\meta{origin}{docs/research/profiles/AR1.md}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Source: the arena dry run \src{docs/research/profiles/AR1.md}, [the profiling session](ses-JRSD). The complete arena test set of 270 tests and Mathlib were run with the arena run line in an arena-shaped container on the aarch64 development host: 8 performance cores, 16 GB, no network, 4 workers, a cold process, batch load, native image. Instruction counts repeat to 0.2 percent. The places are a projection: RLVM has never been measured on the x86-64 runner, and the counts were converted with the ratio that a leader measured in the same session shows between this host and the published board, 0.90 to 1.05.}
\table{
\tr{\th{Configuration}\th{Mathlib, instructions}\th{Times nano-lean}\th{Wall clock}\th{Projected place on the board}}
\tr{\td{reference engine, the arena definition as it was}\td{8,427.1 G}\td{23.33}\td{177.7 s}\td{15}}
\tr{\td{machine, \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}}\td{2,978.5 G}\td{8.25}\td{61.3 s}\td{8}}
\tr{\td{machine, the candidate default set}\td{2,747.7 G}\td{7.61}\td{56.8 s}\td{8, or 7 at the edge of the range}}
\tr{\td{machine with \code{\verb~|facts,probes~} and the two proof-comparison shortcuts}\td{1,977.0 G}\td{5.47}\td{not taken in a quiet window}\td{6}}
\tr{\td{nano-lean v0.4.2}\td{361.2 G}\td{1.00}\td{29.5 s}\td{1}}
\tr{\td{gruszka}\td{419.1 G}\td{1.16}\td{20.0 s}\td{2}}
}
\ul{
\li{No wrong accept and no wrong reject in any configuration. With the reference engine RLVM gives the published verdict of the official checker on 268 of the 270 tests; the other two are [the tests on which the official checker does not terminate](ex-9ECC).}
\li{What costs places is nothing but the Mathlib count. A single wrong reject would put an entry behind all 27 checkers that have neither a wrong accept nor a wrong reject, whatever its speed.}
\li{Places 5 and better are not reachable by switching on anything that exists. Place 4 would need the cost per machine operation to fall by a factor of about 3 on top of the shortcuts; see [the cost of one machine operation](prob-28KQ).}
\li{Small terms of the count: the loader costs 133.2 G, 21 instructions per input byte against 6 for the leaders; admission 25.1 G against under 3 G; garbage collection 0.6 G with the machine.}
\li{With the switch set \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} the test \code{\verb~|perf/loop-unfolded-once~}, [described here](ex-IIVH), takes 31.6 s of its 40 s limit on this host and would probably time out on the slower runner.}
}
\p{This is information, not a target: the arena metric is not the project metric, see [the arena clock](ins-0Q3P).}
\p{See also: [the decision for warm wall clock](dec-7QMU).}
